# Out-of-band control of the running FSM. Separate from the RunSequence
# action so a client that did not own the goal (the web dashboard, the
# Android app) can still pause or stop.

string command
# "pause"       RUNNING -> PAUSED, at the next step boundary (does not cut a
#               trajectory mid-flight)
# "resume"      PAUSED -> RUNNING
# "step"        PAUSED only: run exactly one step, then hold in PAUSED
# "stop" / "cancel" stop now - cancels the in-flight ExecuteSkill goal and returns to IDLE
# "clear_fault" FAULT -> IDLE (sets motors_enabled false to force re-enable on next goal)
# "enter_teach" IDLE -> TEACHING (rejected unless control mode is torque)
# "exit_teach"  TEACHING -> IDLE
# "abort_to_home" cancels now (like "cancel"), then once actually stopped
#               automatically runs "builtin:action_01" (home both arms).
#               From IDLE, homes immediately (nothing to cancel). Refused
#               from FAULT|TEACHING - clear_fault/exit_teach first.
# "enable"      Re-activates the physical hardware components (see
#               motor_enable_client.hpp) so they resend "enable" over CAN -
#               needed after a physical E-stop press+release, which cuts
#               driver power without ros2_control ever seeing it, so it
#               still reports the component as "active" the whole time.
#               Sets motors_enabled true in FsmState on success. Usually not
#               called directly: submitting a run_sequence goal while
#               motors_enabled is false does this automatically first (see
#               RobotSupervisor::handleAccepted()).
---
bool success
string message
